msgid "Localization"
msgstr ""

msgid "For developers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you change a string in a template or in a web server, you have to "
"generate again the file :gh_blob:`cms/locale/cms.pot`. To do so, run this"
" command from the root of the repository."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you have a new translation, or an update of an old translation, you "
"need to update the ``cms.mo`` files (the compiled versions of the "
"``cms.po`` files). You can run ``python setup.py compile_catalog`` to "
"update the ``cms.mo`` files for all translations (or add the ``-l "
"<code>`` argument to update only the one for a given locale). The usual "
"``python setup.py install`` will do this automatically. Note that, to "
"have the new strings, you need to restart the web server."
msgstr ""

msgid "For translators"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To begin translating to a new language, run this command from the root of"
" the repository."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Right after that, open the newly created "
":file:`cms/locale/<code>/LC_MESSAGES/cms.po` and fill the information in "
"the header. To translate a string, simply fill the corresponding msgstr "
"with the translations. You can also use specialized translation softwares"
" such as poEdit and others."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the developers update the ``cms.pot`` file, you do not need to start"
" from scratch. Instead, you can create a new ``cms.po`` file that merges "
"the old translated string with the new, to-be-translated ones. The "
"command is the following, run inside the root of the repository."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"After you are done translating the messages, please run the following "
"command and check that no error messages are reported (the developers "
"will be glad to assist you if any of them isn't clear):"
msgstr ""

